{"abstract":[{"text":"Send records to Aptabase, in its cloud or on your own server, through its events API.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" makes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") for Aptabase in one call. It checks your app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"key and takes the region from it: an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-EU-"},{"text":" key posts to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/eu.aptabase.com\/api\/v0\/events"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-US-"},{"text":" key to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/us.aptabase.com\/api\/v0\/events"},{"text":", and a self-hosted ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"A-SH-"},{"text":" key to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/api\/v0\/events"},{"text":" under the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"host"},{"text":" you pass. The key goes in each request’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"App-Key"},{"text":" header field,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" writes the body. Each batch is split to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": 25 events a request, the most Aptabase takes, and 1,000,000","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes a request, the encoder’s own bound, under the 1 MiB that nginx takes by default in front of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many self-hosted servers. A batch with no record the encoder can write, an empty one included,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"makes no request. The destination retries no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any other status. That includes 418, which Aptabase answers when a request’s body arrives slower","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than 60 bytes a second after a 10-second grace period, as over a poor connection, so those records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are reported as rejected rather than retried. No trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves this module out, so import","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"What Aptabase does with these events depends on more than the events themselves:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase counts users itself. Its server hashes each request’s IP address and ","type":"text"},{"code":"User-Agent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header field with a salt it changes every day, so a user is one network address and client on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one day. The destination sends no user or device identifier; it can’t keep the server from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seeing the address a request comes from.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase looks up each request’s IP address and stores its country and region with every event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the request, so its dashboard breaks counts down by where the requests came from."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its sessions are the sessions enricher’s. A record with no session, such as one a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recovered after a relaunch, counts as a session of one event."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Its breakdowns by operating system, app version, build, device model and locale come from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard context. Give the tracker the standard context enrichers, or those breakdowns are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty. A recovered record keeps no context, so it shows none of them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"text":" decides where events go. Aptabase shows events marked as debug events only in its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Debug mode, apart from your users’ events, and keeps them for months rather than years.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Aptabase requires an ","type":"text"},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with every event, and keeps it, but its events dashboard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t show it. The destination always sends ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The app key is public, as Aptabase’s own SDKs ship it inside every app, and the events API takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no other credential, so the destination builds on every platform and an app sends to Aptabase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directly."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import AptabaseEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let aptabase = try HTTPDestination.aptabase(","    appKey: appKey,  \/\/ from the app's Instructions page: A-EU-…, A-US-… or A-SH-…","    isDebug: false,  \/\/ true for builds whose events only Debug mode should show","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions(), .application(), .device(), .operatingSystem(), .locale()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: aptabase)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a self-hosted server, pass the URL it is reached at as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"host"},{"type":"text","text":", such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https:\/\/aptabase.example.com"},{"type":"text","text":", with a path where it is served under one; the destination appends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/api\/v0\/events"},{"type":"text","text":". A host must be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseSetupError","type":"reference"},{"text":": for a key that is empty or only whitespace; for one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that isn’t ","type":"text"},{"code":"A-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a region, ","type":"text"},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a body of ASCII letters and digits; for a region other than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"EU","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"SH","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"DEV","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", in capitals; for a self-hosted key without a host, or a cloud key with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one; and for a host that isn’t a plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" URL, or that already ends in the endpoint. A key of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a server run in development (","type":"text"},{"code":"A-DEV-","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is taken as a self-hosted one, so it needs the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"development server’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"https","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" URL as ","type":"text"},{"code":"host","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Aptabase’s SDKs default to ","type":"text"},{"code":"http:\/\/localhost:3000","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for such a key, which the factory refuses, so serve the development server over TLS. ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no default:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for builds whose events only Debug mode should show, such as debug builds.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Sessions","text":"Sessions"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","text":" is the record’s session, from the sessions enricher: its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a lowercase UUID. Nothing else identifies a record: no vendor identifier, device identifier or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account, and no trace context. A record with no session has its own identifier as its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","text":": making up a session would join unrelated records, skipping the record would lose it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and Aptabase takes no event without a session."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"What-Aptabase-receives","text":"What Aptabase receives"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each request is a JSON array of events. Every event has:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eventName"},{"type":"text","text":", the event’s name;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"sessionId","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the session;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timestamp"},{"type":"text","text":", the record’s timestamp in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, so an event sent late still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"counts at the time it was tracked;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"systemProps","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"osName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"osVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"appVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"appBuildNumber","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"locale","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the locale’s language and region (","type":"text"},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), each when the record’s context has it;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isDebug","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as you pass it; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"sdkVersion","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A context value longer than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Aptabase takes (30 characters of the system’s name, 100 of its version, 50 of the app’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"version, 20 of its build and 100 of the device’s model) is left out and the event is sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without it, as Aptabase would refuse the whole request. A long build number such as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"2026.11.27.1432-abc1234","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is left out of every event the build sends, so its breakdown is empty.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The encoder logs a notice the first time it leaves out each one;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"props"},{"type":"text","text":", when the event has any to send."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made with. Aptabase keeps strings, numbers and booleans, and only a placeholder for an object or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an array, so an object or array is flattened into dotted names: a "},{"code":"cart","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holding "},{"code":"size","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"cart.size","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the first element of "},{"code":"tags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"tags.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A boolean stays a boolean, which Aptabase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores as "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a number keeps its JSON type; and a "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property is left out. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase stores a number as a .NET "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"decimal"},{"type":"text","text":", so it keeps 28 decimal places and rounds a smaller"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fraction away."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Records-left-out","text":"Records left out"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one the plan doesn’t describe, whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", or that holds a value JSON can’t;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose event name is only whitespace or longer than the 60 characters Aptabase takes, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase refuses the whole request holding one;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one with a property, once flattened, whose name is empty, only whitespace or longer than 40","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters, which Aptabase would drop;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a string value longer than 180 characters, which Aptabase would cut short;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one with a number of magnitude 2⁹⁶ (about 7.9 × 10²⁸) or more, past a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"decimal"},{"type":"text","text":", for which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase fails the whole request;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one whose values flatten to the same name twice;"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"one whose timestamp falls outside the years 1 to 9999;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one tracked more than 23 hours before its batch is encoded, as Aptabase drops an event more than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a day old while answering 200, the hour to spare for a queue on the server and clocks that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disagree;"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"one too large for a request of 1,000,000 bytes on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Characters are counted in UTF-16, as .NET counts them, so an emoji counts two. The destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports each record left out as ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" whose reason is an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError","isActive":true},{"text":". When the destination is made, it logs a notice for each event and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property of the plan whose name would be left out.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A request is encoded once and retried as it is, so each request’s deadline is 23 hours after its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"oldest record was tracked: one still failing by then isn’t sent again, which Aptabase would answer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with 200 while storing nothing. It is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.deadlineExceeded(deadline:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":". A clock that reads NaN or infinite has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every record reported. An event from the future, by a clock that runs ahead, is sent, and Aptabase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stores it at the time it arrives."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 23 hours are measured by the device’s own clock, but Aptabase measures a day by its server’s."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"On a device whose clock runs about a day behind, a record tracked just now carries a timestamp a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"day old: the encoder sends it, and Aptabase drops it while answering 200, so the record is lost"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without a report."}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"What-Aptabase-doesnt-report","text":"What Aptabase doesn’t report"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase answers 200 to a request with a key of no app, of a deleted app, or of an account it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"locked, such as one past its plan’s monthly events, and stores nothing: check that the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"events reach the app’s Live View after setting the destination up. It doesn’t remove duplicates,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so a record sent again, after a retry whose answer was lost or a store’s redelivery, is counted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"twice."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Aptabase takes 20 requests a second from one IP address, and answers 429 past it, which the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination retries on its backoff."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Aptabase receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Aptabase","title":"Sending to Aptabase","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/AptabaseEncodingError"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"AptabaseEncoding","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"AptabaseEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"AptabaseEncoding"},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://AptabaseEncoding/documentation/AptabaseEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/aptabaseencoding\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination\/aptabase(appkey:host:isdebug:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends batches to the Aptabase app of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"appKey"},{"text":", at the region its key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names or, for a self-hosted key, at ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"host"},{"text":", marking every event as a debug event or not as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isDebug"},{"text":" says, through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transport"},{"text":", retrying a send that fails for now with the waits of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clock"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AptabaseEncoding\/documentation\/AptabaseEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:transport:backoff:clock:now:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"aptabase"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"appKey"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"host"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials3URLV","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"isDebug"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV","text":"TrackingPlan"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"transport"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"backoff"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdenti